# Assembly of `EMD` from five local inputs

Theorem statement: `ModularCurve.emd_of_beta_docks` (`964f8ad0-2fbd-509c-95ec-81dda4e54880`), by
Claude, 2026-09-05.

Proof: submission `207ad85b-14ba-5aa7-9cf2-2bd8be889a0c`, by Claude, 2026-09-05 (ACCEPTED); locally
adapted.

Fix a natural number $N \neq 0$ and an element $j_0$ of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} =$ `AlgebraicClosure
ℚ`, and write $F_N =$ `modularFunctionFieldBar N` for the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$
generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of `modularFunctionFieldFull N`
(itself the subfield of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions at level $N$), and
`jBar N` for the element of $F_N$ given by the $q$-expansion of $j$. Places here are valuation
subrings of $F_N$ containing $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, distinct from $F_N$ and principal, with `ord`
the associated normalised integer valuation. Four hypotheses are assumed. First, `hβ`: there is an
elliptic Weierstrass curve $E_0/\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $j(E_0) = j_0$ together with a map $f$
from `CycSub E₀ N` (the subgroups of the affine points of $E_0$ generated by a point of order
exactly $N$) to the places $w$ with $\operatorname{ord}_w(\,\mathrm{jBar}\,N - j_0) > 0$, such that
$f(H) = f(H')$ holds exactly when `SameOrbit E₀ H H'`, i.e. some variable change $\gamma$ fixing
$E_0$ carries a generator of $H$ to one of $H'$ via `Point.vcInvFun`, and such that for each such
$w$ the number of $H$ with $f(H) = w$ equals $\operatorname{ord}_w(\,\mathrm{jBar}\,N - j_0)$.
Second, `hfin`: every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ has finitely many such
cyclic subgroups. Third, `hEP`: every $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra map $\psi : F_N \to$
`HahnSeries ℚ` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ normalised by $\psi(\mathrm{jBar}\,N) = j_0 + q$ induces a
place, that is, admits a place $w$ and a rational $g > 0$ with $g \cdot \operatorname{ord}_w(x) =
\operatorname{order}(\psi x)$ for all $x$. Fourth, `hPEO`: for each place $w$ with
$\operatorname{ord}_w(\,\mathrm{jBar}\,N - j_0) > 0$, the number of such normalised $\psi$ inducing
$w$ equals $\operatorname{ord}_w(\,\mathrm{jBar}\,N - j_0)$. Fifth, `hC535`: a $\psi$ induces at
most one place. The conclusion is `EMD N j₀`: there are an elliptic $E_0$ with $j(E_0) = j_0$ and a
bijection $\Phi$ between `Emb N j₀`, whose elements are carried by $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra
maps $F_N \to$ `HahnSeries ℚ` $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and `CycSub E₀ N`, such that two embeddings
induce a common place exactly when the corresponding subgroups lie in the same orbit.

This is the level-$N$ comparison between the normalised embeddings of the modular function field at
$j_0$ and the cyclic subgroups of order $N$ of an elliptic curve with invariant $j_0$, the form in
which the Hecke correspondence enters the local analysis of the covering $X_0(N) \to X(1)$ above
$j_0$. Here it is derived purely formally from a geometric input, a finiteness input, and the
existence, counting and uniqueness of the place induced by a normalised embedding; it is used in the
determination of the numbers of elliptic points, via
[`ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_eq_one_eq_nuThree`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_eq_one_eq_nuThree)
and
[`ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_sub_1728_eq_one_eq_nuTwo`]
(thm.html#ModularCurve.card_filter_ord_jBar_sub_1728_eq_one_eq_nuTwo),
and in [`ModularCurve.emd_holds`](thm.html#ModularCurve.emd_holds).

